## Item 2: the lily pad cutout from above

- The command of the brief as given (`--canvas 1024x1024 --views three-quarter --el 35`, margin 16)
  fails: `FAIL lily-pad/three-quarter.png ... lowest opaque row 1023, foot row 1008`. A look-down
  camera puts the near rim 117 px below the foot row (acceptance N1), so the pad runs off the
  bottom edge of a margin-16 canvas.
- Final command: `./forge cutout lily-pad --out out/chibi-sprouts/r1/props/high --ppm 1024 --canvas
  1024x1024 --views three-quarter --el 35 --margin 150`.
- Result: `ok lily-pad/three-quarter.png 1024x1024 soft 1357 edge 1142 worstDrop 29% rows
  734..990 cols 306..716`, last line `result ok`. Manifest: ppm 1024, canvas 1024x1024, elevation
  35, footPoint (512, 874).
- I looked at the PNG once. The pad reads as a round green dish with the V notch toward the
  viewer, 9 veins, and the curled rim. The veins are visible, as the brief asks.

## Why commit b3460c68 adds an elevation field to the cutout manifest

The brief did not ask for this field. The check of item 2 cannot pass without it:

1. The cut-out manifest is per folder ("one folder keeps one scale", src/cli/forge.ts:396-400). The
   folder now also records the camera elevation, and one folder keeps one elevation.
2. scripts/cutout-check.mjs reads the elevation. At elevation 0 the rule stays as before: the
   lowest opaque row is the foot row, within 4 px. At elevation above 0 the rule fits the geometry:
   the model must reach the foot row (nothing floats above it) and must not touch the bottom edge
   (the canvas holds the near edge). The old rule cannot hold for a level foot point and a camera
   above it, because the near rim is 117 px below the foot row by geometry.
3. The folder walk now skips a nested folder that has its own manifest. props/high and
   props/presets/* are checked against their own manifest, not against the props manifest.

The change adds a clipping rule. It does not remove a check.

