- a330434d test(cutout): detect a 1 px alpha seam (scripts/cutout-check.mjs,
  tests/cutout.test.ts).
- 51fee130 fix(cutout): read the buffer in strips, so no row is lost (src/render/cutout.ts,
  src/render/page.ts).
- b3460c68 fix(cutout): a look-down folder records its elevation (src/cli/forge.ts,
  scripts/cutout-check.mjs).
- Next: this log, briefs/lily-pad.md, the two acceptance-lily-pad files (added unchanged), and one
  plan sub-bullet.

## Known weak points

- The strip height is 64 raw rows. The fix is proven on 27 PNGs in 4 folders on this GPU (ANGLE
  over gl). A much larger canvas could still lose a row inside a strip. The new seam check would
  report it.
- The seam check needs columns where both neighbours are fully opaque. A seam in a part that is
  only soft on both sides would pass. The check caught 4 of the 4 seams in the old folders.
- The elevated foot rule is new. A later viewer of the gate saw only the level form.
- I did not rate my own work.

